A>asm termxtp1
CP/M ASSEMBLER - v2.01
03F7
005H USE FACTOR
END OF ASSEMBLY

Note: the release file may be named as peachp1.com to show it is the newer  p1 patch update.
Use the appropriate name in the following ddt command line.

A>DDT 		peach.com
DDT VERS 2.2
NEXT  PC
6A00 0100
-itermxtp1.hex
-r
NEXT  PC
6A00 0000
-g0

A>save 106 peach.com
A>

Note: Both the former MagicWand and the newer PeachText both name the editor as "edit.com"
I tend to name edit.com from PeachText as peach.com to avoiod confusion, but you may need to rename it if you wish integration in with the other PeachTree components.

Note: This version of Peachtext was acquired from an Epson QX10 archive and was originally configured for such.

There is one known bug in the conversion to generic CP/M-80 and ANSI VT100 / XTERM escape sequences, that is that the marker character for block start and block end is ignored and the character in the document at the marker point is used. THe block copy functionality workls


Function Keys (PC keyboard)
---------------------------

<cursor> as expected
f1	Line scroll backward
f2	Line scroll forward
Home	Home line/screen
PageUp	Page backward
PageDn	Page forward
Insert	Full insert (open text)
Delete	Delete Character
f5	Set FormFeed character
f6	Start Search/Replace
f7	Repeat Search/Replace
f8	Set Block Marker
f3	Insert character mode (until cursor move)
f4	Delete to end of line (second push)
Ctrl-T	Jump to Top of file
Ctrl-B	Jump to Bottom of file
Ctrl-W	Word delete
BkSpace Delete backwards (if this doesn't work, check and adjust your
        terminal emulator backspace setting)
